# Finite witnesses for the binary G₂ cycle calculation

These tables extend the saved `MatrixData` witnesses with the boundary,
coordinate extraction, two cycle actions, and all eight ambient cycle actions.
Flags and endpoints use the original GAP enumeration (converted to zero-based
indices). Matrices act on columns; packed columns store bit zero first.
`Checks` verifies these data in Lean's kernel. In particular, `retractionColumns`
certifies that every vector killed by the boundary lies in the saved cycle span.

The paired basis consists of the saved half followed by its image under root F.
It allows the assembly owner to prove full derived-group invariance from the
ambient pair permutation. No group identification is asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith G.7.2(3), printed p.348/PDF p.359. Witnesses are from
`GenerateCandidates.g`, `ambient_data.json`, and `prepare_factors.py` in the
retained G2CycleFiltration calculation. Root matrices originate in the ATLAS
ports RootLinearMaps/WeylMaps, revision 8eabb35afe2b5e45bf913a2d05c53e558d2e2917,
copyright 2026 Gerald Höhn and the ATLAS contributors; LICENSES/ATLAS.txt.
-/

